<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Jan-Oct car sales fell 12.3 pct/yr - ago.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Jan-Oct car sales fell 12.3 pct/yr - ago.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Car and truck sales in Colombia fell 12.3 percent in the first 10 months of 1996 compared to the same period last year, according to a closely watched report on the status of the country's auto trade.</p>
<p>The report, issued by GM Colmotores, the local subsidiary of General Motors, said sales had fallen 4.2 percent in October and that imported vehicles accounted for 34.6 percent of all cars and trucks sold during the month.</p>
<p>-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
</text>
